  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Heads up – call out the fingers",
  "description": "Everyone has a ball and dribbles freely in the half court, in every direction and without bumping into anyone. The coach stands at the half-court line and holds up some fingers. Everyone calls out the number as soon as they see it, and the coach changes it straight away. Anyone who is silent or calls the wrong number was looking at the ball. The coach can move along the half-court line so the players have to find them.\n\nThen add a task to the signal: call the number, then crossover and change direction. A closed fist means change of pace: two quick, long dribbles forward and then straight back down into a controlled dribble.\n\nVariations: weak hand only; an even number means crossover and an odd number means between the legs; two coaches showing different numbers, and the players call out the sum. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pound the ball into the floor and let your hand feel it – your eyes are busy."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the ball to the side of your body, not straight in front of your feet."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep the crossover low and tight, and take the first step in the new direction right away."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Change of pace: sink as you brake and push off hard when you go."
    }
  ],
